// Title: Suspicious Reg Add BitLocker
// Sigma ID: 0e0255bf-2548-47b8-9582-c0955c9283f5
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-11-15 | Modified: 2022-09-09
// ATT&CK: impact, T1486
// Description: Detects suspicious addition to BitLocker related registry keys via the reg.exe utility
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2021/11/15/exchange-exploit-leads-to-domain-wide-ransomware/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_bitlocker.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "REG" and ProcessCommandLine contains "ADD" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/v" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/f") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "EnableBDEWithNoTPM" or ProcessCommandLine contains "UseAdvancedStartup" or ProcessCommandLine contains "UseTPM" or ProcessCommandLine contains "UseTPMKey" or ProcessCommandLine contains "UseTPMKeyPIN" or ProcessCommandLine contains "RecoveryKeyMessageSource" or ProcessCommandLine contains "UseTPMPIN" or ProcessCommandLine contains "RecoveryKeyMessage")
